# The boot modules (docs/boot.md, "Boot modules"): what the initramfs must load before it
# can find and mount the system partition and userdata, when the kernel builds it as a
# module. build-boot-modules.sh takes them, with their dependencies and soft
# dependencies, from the kernel's modules/<release>/ tree. A name the kernel builds in
# needs nothing. "required": the build fails when the kernel has it neither built in nor
# as a module; the others are drivers a kernel may simply not have.
#
# NAME            [required]
# file systems: the system partition (btrfs), userdata (ext4), the deployment's root (overlay)
btrfs           required
ext4            required
overlay         required
# disks: NVMe (and Intel's VMD in front of it), SATA, virtual machines
vmd
nvme
ahci
ata_piix
sd_mod
virtio_pci
virtio_blk
virtio_scsi
# eMMC and SD cards behind PCI or ACPI
sdhci_pci
sdhci_acpi
mmc_block
# USB disks (an install medium, an external disk)
xhci_pci
ehci_pci
ohci_pci
uhci_hcd
usb_storage
uas
